      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ROCKIN IN PARADISE (7) settled in the leading division and finished well but could only manage third last start over 1660m at Albion Park, failing to emulate his success at this track the run before. Drawn to enjoy an economical run and might sweat on the sprint lane. Finds a suitable assignment and can return to winning form. REDS STAR DEAL (1) has had four runs this campaign and is yet to finish in the top three. Was again unable to find the frame last time when he finished sixth over 1660m at Albion Park, beaten 15 metres after having raced outside the leader at the bell. No excuses from this advantageous draw. Beautifully placed and is sure to be there at the finish. DOCTA FEELGOOD (2) scored an all of the way win here two runs back, then didn't do a bad job when fourth over 1780m at this track last time out after racing outside the leader at the bell. Each-way chance. CEDAR CREEK FALLS (3) is next best and gets every chance from a favourable draw. Include in combinations.",
